      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts**. \n\nThe page explains that the key is read from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup by a local secrets loader, and then injected only into the child process\u0027s environment\u2014the Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated. This architecture ensures that a compromised Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API. The Query agent follows the same scoping model.",
